\par
## Problem to be solved\par
\par
Leadership wants an autonomous risk and resilience command center. What they have is 18 plants, 5 regions, 8 industry types, and systems that evolved independently (PLC/DCS, SCADA/HMI, historian, SIS, CMMS/EAM, SOC/SIEM, IAM/PAM, vendor access, engineering workstations).\par
\par
The operating failure is this: **no one can produce a defensible cyber-physical picture**. Inventories disagree about what exists. Telemetry disagrees about what is happening. Vulnerability scores disagree with process consequence. Safety records disagree with field work. Backup flags disagree with restore reality. SOC isolation advice can conflict with process-safe operation.\par
\par
The goal is **not** to automate control. It is to establish trustworthy situational awareness, contextual risk, resilience decisions, and governed recommendations.\par
\par
## What we are being asked\par
\par
Brownfield forensics **before** AI:\par
\par
- Map current state without treating CMDB, passive discovery, historian, SCADA, CMMS, SIEM, or operator notes as authoritative by name.\par
- Separate **observed**, **registered**, **operational interpretation**, **safety**, and **decision authority**.\par
- Reconcile identity, telemetry quality, process dependencies, contextual risk, safety/security conflicts, and recovery.\par
- Define bounded autonomy, TEVV/evals, KPI before/after, a 90-day roadmap, and an executive defense.\par
- Do not write to controllers, change SIS, bypass interlocks, or isolate without human authority.\par
\par
## Pain points\par
\par
| Pain | Evidence in this repo |\par
|---|---|\par
| No trusted inventory | 200 ACTIVE assets observed OFFLINE/UNSEEN; 343 unknown owners; shadow spreadsheet covers 220 of 2,016 assets; 5 colliding aliases |\par
| Alerts without process meaning | 1,735 of 2,800 alerts have process context UNKNOWN (525 of those HIGH/CRITICAL) |\par
| CVSS theater | Legacy rank sorts by CVSS; 53 CVSS\f2\u8805?\f0 9.0 findings are unreachable; 87 open reachable findings sit on CRITICAL assets |\par
| Safety-blind cyber response | HIGH/CRITICAL \f2\u8594?\f0  `ISOLATE`; handover says do not isolate near minimum stable load |\par
| Ticket vs field | 244 CMMS CLOSED but not returned to service; 161 open/in-progress already returned; 94 temp bypasses |\par
| Recovery theater | 108 of 119 CURRENT backups have restore tests older than 90 days; median restore-test age **379 days** |\par
| Shadow operations | Vendor VPNs, service laptops, `FINAL_v8` spreadsheet, expired risk acceptances (131 of 180) |\par
\par
## End goal / target state\par
\par
A governed command center that can answer, with evidence and uncertainty:\par
\par
1. What asset is this, across aliases and sources?\par
2. What is observed vs registered, and how fresh is that?\par
3. What process unit and downstream consequence does it sit on?\par
4. Which safety barriers are actually active, bypassed, or overdue?\par
5. What is reachable, compensated, and recoverable?\par
6. What action is allowed at which authority tier?\par
\par
Target capabilities that are justified by this evidence: canonical identity, provenance-aware telemetry, process/recovery graphs, contextual risk, safety-aware response policy, HITL on consequential acts, TEVV, and measurable KPIs. Knowledge graphs, RAG, and digital twins are **optional**, not assumed.\par
\par
## Moonshots (possible, not assumed)\par
\par
**Safe to explore after evals:** read-only replay/twin of CASCADE-001 with uncertainty bands; predictive degradation only on GOOD-quality tags; an evidence graph where correlation IDs actually exist; agents limited to observe / correlate / summarize / rank / recommend.\par
\par
**Out of scope:** closed-loop isolation from SIEM severity; PLC writes; setpoint changes; SIS edits; interlock bypass; trip suppression; auto-restart after restore.\par
\par
## How to get there\par
\par
Inventory \f2\u8594?\f0  topology \f2\u8594?\f0  identity \f2\u8594?\f0  telemetry quality \f2\u8594?\f0  process dependencies \f2\u8594?\f0  cyber/safety context \f2\u8594?\f0  recovery graph \f2\u8594?\f0  authority model \f2\u8594?\f0  evals \f2\u8594?\f0  bounded recommenders.\par
\par
| Phase | Window | Exit gate |\par
|---|---|---|\par
| Preserve evidence | Days 1\f1\endash 7 | Baseline KPIs frozen; do not \ldblquote clean\rdblquote  intentional contradictions |\par
| Identity | Days 8\endash 21 | Every asset has a canonical ID **or** an explicit conflict record |\par
| Topology + telemetry | Days 15\endash 35 | Undocumented live paths are first-class; BAD samples cannot be treated as facts |\par
| Process + safety | Days 28\endash 50 | Isolation advice carries safe-state / process consequence or is refused |\par
| Contextual risk + recovery | Days 40\endash 65 | The three expected-fail tests (CVSS rank, backup=ready, always-isolate) flip to pass |\par
| Authority + evals | Days 55\endash 80 | Golden cases EVAL-001..006 plus outage/adversarial cases |\par
| Bounded recommenders | Days 70\endash 90 | Observe\f2\u8594?\f0 recommend only; KPI before/after; no control writes |\par
\par
