\par
## Eight-lens analysis\par
\par
### 1. Imperfection \f1\emdash  defective logic that still runs\par
\par
The production ranking code is simplistic on purpose and is still the decision machinery:\par
\par
- Risk rank = sort by CVSS.\par
- Recovery ready = `backup_status == CURRENT`.\par
- Containment = HIGH/CRITICAL \f2\u8594?\f0  `ISOLATE`.\par
\par
Those three are locked as expected-fail tests. Packaging is also imperfect: package/API version is 2.0.0, `__version__` is 0.1.0, the data manifest still titles the dataset v1. The telemetry schema omits `ingest_time`, `asset_id`, and `source` even though the JSONL carries them. `generate_data.py` does not generate data; it only checks files exist. 1,133 assets have backups older than 180 days; 51 tags are historian-disabled.\par
\par
**Effect:** wrong actions look automated and confident.\par
\par
### 2. Inconsistency \f1\emdash  locally true, globally false\par
\par
Registered state uses ACTIVE/UNKNOWN/RETIRED. Observed state uses ONLINE/OFFLINE/UNSEEN/INTERMITTENT. They are different languages, so naive equality fails on all 2,016 assets. The honest operational conflict set is **200** ACTIVE assets that are OFFLINE or UNSEEN.\par
\par
Also inconsistent: Asset API v1 vs v2 field names; CMMS vs field status (244 + 161); vulnerability **severity labels vs CVSS** (144 HIGH with CVSS &lt; 7, 143 LOW with CVSS \f2\u8805?\f0  7); 47 temperature samples in \'b0F against engineering unit \'b0C; 407 enterprise events received before they occurred; SAFETY_PLC sitting outside L0/L1 (89); sensors/PLCs in DMZ; HMIs in L0.\par
\par
**Effect:** every system can be \ldblquote right\rdblquote  in its own schema and still be unusable for a decision.\par
\par
### 3. Friction \f1\emdash  cost of assembling one decision\par
\par
Nine enterprise sources emit 6,500 events; **half have no correlation ID**. Mean historian ingest delay is 120 seconds; 23,414 of 31,224 samples arrive more than 60 seconds late. Remote access is four parallel methods (jump host, vendor VPN, RDP, service laptop). Night-shift truth is an email. CASCADE-001 is the friction scenario in one timeline: firmware advisory \f2\u8594?\f0  unknown firmware \f2\u8594?\f0  unexpected write \f2\u8594?\f0  vendor session \f2\u8594?\f0  historian deviation \f2\u8594?\f0  operator alarm \f2\u8594?\f0  safety bypassed \f2\u8594?\f0  SOC says isolate \f2\u8594?\f0  process says that may destablize the unit.\par
\par
**Effect:** time-to-cyber-physical confidence is long; SOC and operations argue from different clocks and different worlds.\par
\par
### 4. Complexity \f1\emdash  no single playbook survives a site\par
\par
18 plants, 7 legacy / 5 modernizing / 6 mixed, 13 asset types, 10 protocols, 815 firmware strings, 216 process units, four different safe states, 19 units with **no manual mode**, eight recovery components \f0\'d7 18 plants, five action-authority tiers, twelve analysis layers, timezones from UTC\f2\u8722?\f0 5 to UTC+8.\par
\par
**Effect:** a global rule (especially \ldblquote isolate on HIGH\rdblquote ) is operationally unsafe at some units by construction.\par
\par
### 5. Volatility \f1\emdash  baselines rot inside a shift\par
\par
129 assets are INTERMITTENT. Alert mix includes unexpected writes (404), config drift (388), new devices (399). 94 work orders carry a temporary bypass. 26 safety barriers are bypassed, 35 degraded. Vendor firmware work completes before the ticket updates. Work-order notes include \ldblquote parts substituted\rdblquote  and \ldblquote operator workaround active.\rdblquote\par
\par
**Effect:** an inventory snapshot taken this morning is not the incident picture at 08:55.\par
\par
### 6. Uncertainty \emdash  unknown is a first-class state\par
\par
Unknown owners 343; registered UNKNOWN 122; vuln reachability UNKNOWN 344; compensating control UNKNOWN 235 / NONE 222; safety bypass authorization UNKNOWN 157; remote approval UNKNOWN 76; MFA UNKNOWN 72; recovery backup UNKNOWN 9; alert process context UNKNOWN 1,735; telemetry UNCERTAIN 2,743 + BAD 1,351 = **13.1%**.\par
\par
Eval cases already forbid assuming CMDB is correct and require uncertainty in time reconstruction.\par
\par
**Effect:** a score without confidence is a lie. Every recommendation must carry freshness and uncertainty.\par
\par
### 7. Hidden dependency \emdash  blast radius that diagrams omit\par
\par
**779** network paths are undocumented **and** observed in the last 24 hours. 168 observed paths are explicitly unapproved. 51 process dependencies are undocumented; **33 of those are critical**. 29 recovery records have unverified dependencies. The architecture note names the parallel estate: vendor VPNs, service laptops, spreadsheets, shift notes, stale diagrams. Shadow risk-acceptance and `ot_asset_inventory_FINAL_v8.csv` are not even in `manifest.json`\rquote s file list, so a naive pipeline never sees them. 19 units cannot go to manual \emdash  **network isolation is a process action**, not only a cyber action.\par
\par
**Effect:** isolation and restore have unmodeled consequences. Compensating \ldblquote controls assumed\rdblquote  on 44 risk acceptances is not a control.\par
\par
### 8. Unknown unknown \emdash  what sensing cannot confirm or deny\par
\par
Shadow inventory is 11% coverage; the handover claims it is **newer** than CMDB for a new gateway, so the unknown is which assets exist only there, only in CMDB, or in neither. CASCADE-001 has six controllers with unknown firmware after a family advisory. Historian pressure was flat ~20 minutes while HMI moved \emdash  two sensors of the same process, no adjudicator. Colliding aliases mean identity is not unique. 399 NEW_DEVICE alerts are discovery the inventories did not predict. Anything not in these files (rogue serial links, oral standing orders, contractor jump boxes) is definitionally absent.\par
\par
**Effect:** absence of a record is not absence of a device or a path. Keep an unknown-unknown register; do not impute completeness.\par
\par
